module main

-- §8.3: the bare dotted form `import a.b.c` is disambiguated after module
-- discovery. Here BOTH interpretations are resolvable — module a.b.c
-- exists AND module a.b exports an item `c` — so the form is a
-- compile-time error. (The spec names no diagnostic family;
-- E_NAME_AMBIGUOUS is the closest registered code.)
import a.b.c --!! E_NAME_AMBIGUOUS

--! assertErrorCount 1
-- STATUS(a51e1bf): FAIL — no ambiguity error; the compiler silently prefers the singleton-item interpretation of the bare dotted form
